-c class=\"mjx-c32\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn></mjx-script></mjx-msup></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"INNER\"><mo data-mjx-texclass=\"OPEN\" symmetric=\"true\">‖</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>v</mi><mo data-mjx-texclass=\"CLOSE\" symmetric=\"true\">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"INNER\"><mo data-mjx-texclass=\"OPEN\" symmetric=\"true\">‖</mo><mi>u</mi><mo data-mjx-texclass=\"CLOSE\" symmetric=\"true\">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"INNER\"><mo data-mjx-texclass=\"OPEN\" symmetric=\"true\">‖</mo><mi>v</mi><mo data-mjx-texclass=\"CLOSE\" symmetric=\"true\">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container></span> in a\ncomplex inner product space, then <span class=\"math inline\"><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"CHTML\" style=\"font-size: 113.1%; position: relative;\" data-tex=\"u\n\\perp v\"><mjx-math class=\" MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D462 TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\" space=\"4\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c22A5\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\" space=\"4\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D463 TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>u</mi><mo>⊥</mo><mi>v</mi></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container></span>. Justify your answer.</li>\n</ol>\n</div>","file":"ch11-inner-products/01-inner-products.html"}